# Line endings.
#
# Everything here runs on macOS, so it is LF. A shell script with carriage returns in it
# does not run there at all — bash reads the \r as part of the command — and editing one
# from Windows is enough to rewrite a whole file's endings without saying so.
*           text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.png       binary
*.icns      binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
*.ttc       binary
*.mid       binary
*.dmg       binary
